  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "“Lifestyle” is not a single chain scale—it ranges from compact select-service hotels to luxury, food-and-beverage-driven properties. For urban projects in the United States and Canada, the following brands commonly appear on initial positioning and brand-shortlist exercises.\n\n### Compact, select-service and affordable lifestyle\n\n- **Marriott:** Moxy, Aloft, citizenM  \n- **Hilton:** Motto by Hilton  \n- **Hyatt:** Caption by Hyatt  \n- **IHG:** Ruby  \n- **Choice:** Cambria Hotels, Radisson RED  \n- **Other operators:** YOTEL, Arlo, citizenM-style independent concepts  \n\nThese are particularly relevant for expensive urban sites because they emphasize efficient guestrooms, activated communal space and relatively lean operations. Moxy specifically targets urban/metro development, while citizenM joined Marriott in 2025; IHG is positioning Ruby for the U.S. urban micro-hotel segment. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/ResourceFiles/common-image/moxy-mea-fact-sheet-v3-220622.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Upscale, neighborhood-oriented lifestyle\n\n- **Marriott:** AC Hotels by Marriott, Aloft, Moxy  \n- **Hilton:** Canopy by Hilton, Tempo by Hilton, Graduate by Hilton  \n- **Hyatt:** Hyatt Centric, JdV by Hyatt  \n- **IHG:** Hotel Indigo, Kimpton Hotels & Restaurants, voco  \n- **Choice:** Cambria Hotels, Radisson RED  \n- **Accor/Ennismore:** The Hoxton, Mama Shelter, 21c Museum Hotels, TRIBE  \n- **Independent/operator-led:** Ace Hotel, Virgin Hotels, LINE Hotels, Proper Hotels, Palihotel, Aparium-managed concepts  \n\nThis is usually the broadest competitive group for downtown, mixed-use, entertainment-district and adaptive-reuse projects. Hilton formally groups Canopy, Tempo, Motto, Graduate, Curio and Tapestry within or alongside its lifestyle platform, while IHG’s principal lifestyle candidates include Kimpton, Hotel Indigo and its conversion-oriented collections. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/releases/hilton-set-to-double-lifestyle-portfolio-to-700-hotels-within-next-four-years?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Upper-upscale and luxury lifestyle\n\n- **Marriott:** W Hotels, EDITION, Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, Design Hotels  \n- **Hilton:** NoMad, Curio Collection, LXR Hotels & Resorts  \n- **Hyatt:** Thompson Hotels, Andaz, The Standard, Dream Hotels, The Unbound Collection  \n- **IHG:** Kimpton, Vignette Collection  \n- **Accor/Ennismore:** Mondrian, SLS, Delano, SO/, Hyde, The Hoxton  \n- **Other operators:** Pendry, 1 Hotels, Proper Hotels, Virgin Hotels, Nobu Hotels, Viceroy  \n\nThese are generally evaluated when the site can support destination food and beverage, higher design expenditure, suites or residences, and upper-upscale or luxury average rates. Marriott identifies W and EDITION as luxury-lifestyle brands; Hyatt’s current lifestyle portfolio includes Andaz, Thompson, The Standard, Dream, JdV and Bunkhouse. ([marriott.gcs-web.com](https://marriott.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/marriott-international-announces-outstanding-global-growth-and?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Soft brands and collections\n\nFor conversions, historic buildings or owner-created concepts, developers often compare:\n\n- **Marriott:** Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, Luxury Collection, Design Hotels  \n- **Hilton:** Curio Collection, Tapestry Collection, LXR  \n- **Hyatt:** JdV by Hyatt, The Unbound Collection  \n- **IHG:** Vignette Collection  \n- **Choice:** Ascend Hotel Collection, Radisson Individuals  \n- **Accor:** MGallery, Handwritten Collection  \n- **Wyndham:** Registry Collection, Trademark Collection  \n- **BWH Hotels:** WorldHotels collections, BW Premier Collection, BW Signature Collection  \n\nSoft brands preserve more of the property’s individual identity while providing access to reservation, distribution and loyalty systems. They are especially common in adaptive reuse and existing-hotel repositionings. IHG explicitly markets Vignette as an option for independent luxury and lifestyle hotels, while Choice positions Ascend and Radisson Individuals alongside its upscale portfolio. ([ihgplc.com](https://www.ihgplc.com/en/news-and-media/news-releases/2025/ihg-hotels-and-resorts-conversion-friendly-brands-fuel-growth-opportunities-for-owners?utm_source=openai))\n\n## Practical “first-call” shortlist\n\nFor a typical urban feasibility study, a manageable initial list would often be:\n\n1. **Moxy**\n2. **AC Hotels**\n3. **citizenM**\n4. **Canopy**\n5. **Motto**\n6. **Tempo**\n7. **Hyatt Centric**\n8. **JdV by Hyatt**\n9. **Hotel Indigo**\n10. **Kimpton**\n11. **Cambria**\n12. **Radisson RED**\n13. **Autograph Collection**\n14. **Curio Collection**\n15. **Tribute Portfolio or Tapestry Collection**\n\nFor a higher-end project, add **Thompson, Andaz, W, EDITION, The Standard, Pendry, 1 Hotels, Mondrian and SLS**.\n\nIn Canada, the practical shortlist is often weighted more heavily toward the large-system brands because of distribution, lender recognition and development support. Actual availability depends on market protection, key count, room dimensions, food-and-beverage program, construction cost, conversion condition and whether the brand will approve that specific city and submarket.",
